.TH TILED2VIRCON 1 "October 11, 2026" "Vircon32 DevTools 26.04.24" "Vircon32 Development Tools"
.SH NAME
tiled2vircon \- convert Tiled tile map layers into Vircon32 data files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tiled2vircon
.RB [ \-o
.IR folder/ ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.I map.tmx
.br
.B tiled2vircon
.B \-\-help
.br
.B tiled2vircon
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tiled2vircon
reads a tile map saved by the Tiled map editor
.RI ( https://www.mapeditor.org )
in its XML format
.RI ( .tmx )
and writes every tile layer to its own binary file,
.IR LayerName.vmap ,
named after the layer. A
.I .vmap
file has no header: it is the layer's tiles as little-endian 32-bit
integers, row by row from the top-left, which is exactly the memory
layout of a C array
.BI int[ height ][ width ]\c
\&. A program includes it in the cartridge with the C compiler's
.B embedded
declaration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
embedded int[ 30 ][ 40 ] level1 = "obj/Ground.vmap";
\&...
int tile = level1[ y ][ x ];
.fi
.RE
.PP
Each tile is stored as its index within the map's first tileset: the
Tiled tile id minus that tileset's
.BR firstgid ,
so the tileset's first tile is 0. The map must store its layers in
.B CSV
encoding (Tiled's
.I "Tile Layer Format: CSV"
map property); other encodings are not decoded.
.PP
.B tiled2vircon
prints a line for every layer it saves, even without
.BR \-v ,
and a warning when a layer holds a different number of tiles than the
map's width times its height.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " folder/"
Write the files into
.IR folder .
The folder must already exist, and its name must end with a path
separator: the layer name is appended to it as given, so
.B "\-o obj"
writes
.IR objGround.vmap .
Without
.BR \-o ,
the files go into the current directory.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose: report the output folder.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and author, and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All layers were written.
.TP
.B 1
Any error, printed as
.IR "tiled2vircon: error: description" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR compile (1),
.BR joinpngs (1),
.BR png2vircon (1)
.SH BUGS
An empty cell (Tiled id 0) is written as 0, the same value as the
tileset's first tile. Reserve the first tile as a blank one if empty
cells must be told apart.
.PP
Tiles flipped or rotated in Tiled carry flag bits in the top of their
id, which are not decoded; such tiles do not come out as their tile
index. Only the first
tileset's
.B firstgid
is used, so maps with several tilesets get one continuous numbering
from the first.
.SH AUTHOR
The Vircon32 Tiled importer was written by Javier Carracedo
.RI ( Carra ).
This manual page was written by Matthew Haas for the v32c++ project.
